dnstap-bgp intercepts DNS replies via DNSTap and announces the
resolved IP addresses over BGP. Use it on OPNsense 26.7 (FreeBSD 15.1)
to steer traffic by domain name instead of static prefixes.

Default paths:
  /usr/local/etc/dnstap-bgp/dnstap-bgp.conf
  /usr/local/etc/dnstap-bgp/domains.txt
  /usr/local/etc/rc.d/dnstap_bgp
  /usr/local/etc/rc.conf.d/dnstap_bgp
  /usr/local/sbin/dnstap-bgp
  /var/db/dnstap-bgp/cache.db
  /var/run/dnstap-bgp/dnstap.sock

The service starts in a VNET jail (dtap) by default, the FreeBSD analog
of Linux ip netns, so FRR/BIRD on the host can peer across an epair
(192.168.113.1 host / 192.168.113.2 jail).

Install:
  pkg add os-dnstap-bgp-VERSION.pkg
  sysrc dnstap_bgp_enable=YES
  service dnstap_bgp start

Reload the domain list:
  service dnstap_bgp reload
